{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nFound while verifying d724 AC10 on Windows sweep run 35551741150 (2026-09-21). `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_opcert_signing_key_is_isolated_per_store` fails on the Windows runner. The runner has no OpenSSH that `rebar.attest.sshsig.ssh_keygen_version()` can find, and op-cert signing needs OpenSSH 8.9 or newer. Not a d724 defect class.\n\n## Checked (2026-10-25)\nThe job log for that run (job 106187634058) ends the test with `rebar.attest.sshsig.SshKeygenUnavailable: ssh-keygen (OpenSSH) not found; SSHSIG requires OpenSSH >= 8.9`, so the ticket's cause holds. The same cause fails 24 distinct tests in 5 modules in that log (this test, 11 in test_opcert_local_verify_binding.py, 9 in test_attestation_invalidation.py, 2 in test_opcert_binding_thread_propagation_ff4a.py, 1 in test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py). Three other opcert modules already skip on the same condition with a module-level `_SSH_OK` probe built on `sshsig.ensure_available()`.\n\n## Decision (user, 2026-10-25)\nSkip the test with a clear reason when OpenSSH is older than 8.9 or missing; do not change the Windows workflow. Per-store key isolation stays untested on Windows until a runner has OpenSSH 8.9 or newer.\n\n## Plan\nIn `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` only:\n1. Add a small helper `_skip_without_sshsig()` that calls `sshsig.ensure_available()` and turns `sshsig.SshKeygenUnavailable` (and only that) into `pytest.skip` with a reason that names the exception text and says per-store opcert key isolation is not asserted.\n2. Call it first in `test_opcert_signing_key_is_isolated_per_store`. No module-level skip: the other tests in this module do not need ssh.\n3. Add unit tests of the helper: missing ssh (version None) and an old one (8, 8) skip with the 8.9 floor in the reason; (8, 9) does not skip; any other exception propagates.\nRed proof first: with a PATH shim whose `ssh -V` prints `OpenSSH_8.8p1`, run the real test; before the change it fails with SshKeygenUnavailable (the Windows failure, reproduced on this host), after it reports skipped.\n\nOut of scope: the other 23 failing tests in 4 modules (follow-up task), provisioning OpenSSH on the runner, and `ssh_keygen_version()` probing `ssh -V` rather than `ssh-keygen -V`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With a PATH shim whose `ssh -V` reports OpenSSH 8.8, the real test is skipped with a reason naming the 8.9 floor, where before the change the same run failed with SshKeygenUnavailable (checked: both runs of `pytest tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_opcert_signing_key_is_isolated_per_store -rs` recorded in a ticket comment).\n- [ ] With this host's real ssh (OpenSSH 10.3) the same test still runs and passes (checked: the same command without the shim reports 1 passed).\n- [ ] The helper skips for a missing ssh and for 8.8, proceeds for 8.9, and lets any other exception propagate (checked: the new helper tests pass).\n- [ ] Only `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` changes, and no other test in it changes behaviour (checked: `git diff --stat` lists that one file; collected node ids differ only by the new tests).\n- [ ] `make verify` shows no failure outside the known pandoc set, and the Gerrit change is `Verified +1`.\n\n## Testing\n```\npytest tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py -q\nmake verify\n```\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792978026370734001,"uuid":"45ece1e8-f451-4efe-bc03-0a83b0108232"}